# Copy to `.env.local` and set what you need. Nothing here is required to run
# the app: every flag has a default, and the API is reached through the Vite
# proxy in `vite.config.ts` (/api -> http://localhost:3000) rather than a URL
# variable.
#
# These gate the parts of the redesign that depend on API fields the backend
# does not return yet. The rule they follow: a surface that would show INVENTED
# data is visible while it is being built and off in a production build, so the
# work can be reviewed without a guessed number ever reaching a real approver.
# `src/config/features.ts` carries the reasoning for each one.
#
# Accepts exactly "true" or "false"; anything else falls back to the default.


# --- on in development, off in a production build -------------------------

# Sidebar saved views. Needs GET /api/saved-views.
VITE_FEATURE_SAVED_VIEWS=

# Multi-select and the bulk action bar. The actions inside it stay disabled:
# "Approve all" cannot exist as the product stands, because approving requires
# a signature placed on the rendered PDF.
VITE_FEATURE_BULK_ACTIONS=

# Out-of-office and delegated approvals. Needs user.outOfOffice. The Save
# button is disabled until there is an endpoint behind it.
VITE_FEATURE_DELEGATION=


# --- off everywhere until the data is real --------------------------------

# SLA countdowns ("2 days left") and breach figures. Shipped and on: the API
# returns a real dueAt. Nothing appears unless a deadline has been set on the
# server (SLA_DEFAULT_DAYS, or slaDays on a step) - with none set the table
# goes on showing age, which is true. Set to false to hide the countdown even
# where deadlines exist.
VITE_FEATURE_SLA=

# The QUEUE load bar on the people table. Needs a per-user open-step count.
# Deriving it from fetchDocuments under-reports everyone but the signed-in
# user, and a load bar that reads low because of a permission boundary is the
# kind of number a manager reassigns work on.
VITE_FEATURE_APPROVER_LOAD=

# The seal strip on the audit ledger. Shipped and on by default: every audit
# record carries a digest over its own contents and the one before it, and an
# administrator can have the whole chain read back and recomputed. Set it to
# false to hide the strip; it does not turn the seal itself off, which is a
# server concern (LEDGER_SEAL_SECONDS).
VITE_FEATURE_LEDGER_INTEGRITY=

# The preparer's "Skip step" button has NO flag here, deliberately. It follows
# `user.workflowPolicy.allowStepSkip` from GET /api/auth/me, because the
# server's answer is a row an administrator changes on the Workflow policy
# screen and nothing in a compiled bundle can follow a database row. A flag
# that could force it on would only produce a button answered by 403.
# `src/config/features.ts` carries the reasoning.

# The topbar "Live" pill. A pulsing dot labelled "Live" asserts a push
# connection; this app polls on navigation. Turn it on when there is a real
# subscription behind it.
VITE_FEATURE_LIVE=
